From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dlsym on bionic libc's handle finds the process's global symbols too

A native bridge's proxy libc (Berberis) looks each host function up with dlsym on the libc.so handle (libc_bio): functions
Android's libc has but apklayer provides elsewhere (__system_property_* in its runtime) were not found and became Bad thunk aborts.

apklayer patch: 0036 of patches/bionic_translation.
---
--- a/linker/dlfcn.c
+++ b/linker/dlfcn.c
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
  */
 #include <dlfcn.h>
 #include <gelf.h>
+#include <link.h>
 #include <pthread.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
@@ -158,6 +159,14 @@
 			return wrapper_create(symbol, sym);
 		}

+		/* apklayer patch: bionic's libc (libc_bio) answers what Android's libc has and the process provides elsewhere (apklayer's
+		 * __system_property_* store): a native bridge's proxy libc looks its host functions up on this handle */
+		struct link_map *lm = NULL;
+		if (dlinfo(handle, RTLD_DI_LINKMAP, &lm) == 0 && lm && lm->l_name && strstr(lm->l_name, "libc_bio") && (sym = dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT, symbol))) {
+			pthread_mutex_unlock(&apkenv_dl_lock);
+			return wrapper_create(symbol, sym);
+		}
+
 		/* it's not our handle, so unless it's a special value might as well bail now */
 		set_dlerror(DL_ERR_SYMBOL_NOT_FOUND);
 	}
